    "check": "sixteen elected and one defeated; all seventeen printed votes accounted for.",
    "url": "https://www.britishnewspaperarchive.co.uk/viewer/bl/0001123/19390517/130/0008"
  },
  "note": "Election of the Coleraine Borough Council, polled Monday 15 May 1939; seventeen candidates for sixteen seats (Derry Journal, 17 May 1939, p. 8). Seventeen candidates for sixteen seats; nineteen nominations had been received and two were withdrawn. The four candidates topping the poll became aldermen. The report notes newcomers Clements, Ross, Scott, D. J. Christie and Samuel Henry; Gribbon was the retiring member defeated. No party label was printed against any candidate in the result."
